    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_ca4383da",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes a photo of a Black woman speaking about interracial marriage with a photo of a man in a suit, using the text 'hold my hookah pipe!' to imply that she is being 'held' or controlled by the man's perspective. The meme is hateful because it uses a racialized stereotype to mock and demean Black women by implying they are not 'marrying their own kind' and are therefore 'not good enough' or 'not desirable' for interracial unions. This is a direct attack on Black women based on their race and gender, fitting the 'Hateful' category as it targets a protected characteristic (race and gender) with derogatory and degrading implications. The meme also contains misogynous elements by suggesting that Black women are not 'marrying their own kind' and are therefore 'not good enough' or 'not desirable' for interracial unions, which is a harmful stereotype that reinforces racial and gender-based discrimination. The meme is also propagandistic as it seeks to influence opinions about interracial marriage and Black women's choices, and it is harmful as it can cause harm to Black women and their communities by reinforcing negative stereotypes and promoting racial and gender-based discrimination.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d1224537"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
