    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_6dedf08a",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the Black woman as the object being 'held' by the male perspective",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the Black woman in the bottom panel, who is visually and textually framed as the object being 'held' by the male perspective represented by the man in the suit. The phrase 'hold my hookah pipe!' is mapped onto her, implying she is being controlled or objectified by the male viewpoint. This projection is reinforced by the textual material 'too many of our brothers are not marrying our sisters', which positions her as the subject of the male gaze and judgment. The user sees themselves as the one who is 'holding' or controlling the situation, or as the one who is being 'held' by the stereotype, depending on the viewer's interpretation, but the meme's structure forces the viewer to identify with the woman as the object of the male stereotype.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
